main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ array deleted: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
delete\[\] of non-array object: FAILURE
--
"delete[] of non-array object" fails: CBMC's C library malloc (also
calloc and realloc, src/ansi-c/library/stdlib.c) may clear
__CPROVER_malloc_is_new_array but leaves __CPROVER_new_object, the object
of the last new-expression, as it is; delete[] then sees that object
recorded as not an array.  The same with develop (8fcda33365).  Seen in
libc++'s ~basic_filebuf for std::ofstream (cvise reduction).
